  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "2bcf6a1e-129f-4db2-b2ad-2c83a1ab0000"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the region heads, each measured by both; so is every Euclidean head, \
through the support of its vertex density"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"f1f1b0e3-21de-427e-94cb-4a7d3120507f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Ball on the square grid: counting measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"], "+", "2", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "+", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "804b1040-8e4b-4e65-8a9d-2c412f8a062a"],
 ", Riemannian measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"], "-", "2", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "+", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9d0df603-4ee2-4f60-83ee-772e9ef14dd3"],
 ", the counting measure of the ball of radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "-", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "282bb331-dacb-43c0-a4ce-16eebcf646e8"],
 ". The same shift holds on the triangular and hexagonal lattices, before the \
rim, and is the convention of the Wolfram Physics technical introduction."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"33c2682d-7a0a-4414-9fdd-41adf75cda01"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Shell on the square grid: counting measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"4", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ad77916-688e-42d8-9f76-3cd30bfa199f"],
 ", the coordination sequence; Riemannian measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "593f419d-5675-4adb-9656-22162107dc4c"],
 ", since a shell is all boundary."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"19e98007-7a90-41d2-9e69-8b6353716589"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Segment on the square grid between vertices ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ce876272-80ee-4233-acef-05138f2a773d"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dd7f1482-cfff-410a-82d8-e95fe565965e"],
 " steps apart along the two axes, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[GreaterEqual]", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c7ce1be6-1282-4be3-b5ec-601b1daabd15"],
 ": its interval is a rectangle, with counting measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "+", "1"}], ")"}], "(", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], "+", "1"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "de31dd13-a6fd-4a90-9ef3-dd2928f6a2ca"],
 " and Riemannian measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "-", "1"}], ")"}], "(", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], "-", "1"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "895ad5e1-59da-4aca-b219-f93fbf312ff6"],
 "."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"8e74c3be-1abc-46a4-9703-641736783026"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Ball on the discretized plane: the Riemannian measure can exceed the \
counting measure of the smaller ball, when a vertex at distance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "183f7aba-c810-484b-93e6-f7843d55fd44"],
 " has no neighbour at distance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "+", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a90e71df-0101-4654-a36c-da2c6c91623d"],
 "."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"9763ccf7-e159-411d-a632-e48ededcade6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["VolumeGrowthObservables"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/VolumeGrowthObservables", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "78ae1cb9-ef73-4110-8ee2-79299fcca771"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the dimension and the scalar curvature read from the growth of the balls \
under either measure; it lives on the Riemannian Infrageometry guide"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"cf12f45d-6ce8-4277-b473-dd962c2095c7"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Find Functions", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"28b99f60-5136-4048-8217-7ac9823cb6af"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraPoint"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraPoint", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "61d4daf9-49b5-4ee3-93c9-aad07cdb2575"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a vertex drawn from the candidate pool, narrowed by \"From\" and \"Distance\
\"; a trailing count gives a List of vertices"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"a46494a7-2e6b-4263-a7cd-96585fdcdaad"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraMidpoint"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraMidpoint", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "8cb0f253-6447-4468-abec-0ef7fc33203b"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the middle vertices of the shortest paths from p1 to p2 as a density, one \
vertex at even distance, two at odd"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"f4565d6f-8b8a-4fc1-a623-ead5c337c669"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraEquidistantSet"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraEquidistantSet", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "afbfdd5b-cbe3-4059-b049-e16b5357e4b7"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the vertices equidistant from p1, \[Ellipsis], pn, as a sorted vertex list; \
a trailing {lo, hi} thickens each bisector to a slab"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"eeb9d5bb-96bd-451b-8d7f-17d7e49684c0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraSphere"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraSphere", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "b74f7ebf-9344-4771-9d3d-924f7717c27e"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "n inclusion-minimal connected subsets of the shell of c that separate its \
inside from its outside; Properties and Method choose the class and the search"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"885fb02b-789e-4798-b7ee-efd5f81981bb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraSegment"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraSegment", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "c79c8eaf-0813-4aef-b7f1-a277eb8b36cc"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one shortest path from p to q as a vertex list; a trailing count gives a \
List of them"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"28dfd7a2-f156-4fd6-93e6-c69393ee2650"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraRay"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraRay", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "34cc5072-2972-4f06-80fe-7913ae85c590"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one ray from p through q as a vertex list, a shortest path from p through q \
that no neighbour of its last vertex prolongs; a trailing count gives a List \
of them"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"0eb405d9-1324-4b81-afe5-526bd1d25928"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraLine"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraLine", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "631653f3-ab8e-47ed-8a7d-a4c7aecf2868"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one line through p and q as a vertex list, an inextensible shortest path \
through both; a trailing count gives a List of them"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"c405cb95-5df0-474f-be11-e9c8f3068fda"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Measurements", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"e237e636-f36d-42c8-92e7-fbfc6c369e9c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "6ce20b29-c1df-40cb-924a-39faed2f440a"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a property of a head on a graph: \"Graph\", \"Cardinality\", \"Length\", \
\"VertexDensity\", \"EdgeDensity\", \"Subgraph\", \"Faithful\", \
\"CountingMeasure\" and \"RiemannianMeasure\"; a List of properties gives an \
Association, All gives every property"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"f5930c1e-6ab5-4788-870e-13c549e71b13"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraDensity"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraDensity", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "97e57c67-4b0e-469a-9b0e-1a2361782a81"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the marginal of any shape to the vertex set with respect to the counting \
measure: a vertex, a vertex list, a density, a walk graph; the one coercion \
in the API"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"d6d85bca-6d7b-463d-9595-1cd52bf242cf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraRepresentative"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraRepresentative", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "d703b05d-214e-48cf-8435-6313cc5eb1e3"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one member of a head as a vertex list, read off its graph or found by its \
search; a trailing count gives a List of them, \"RandomChoice\" a random \
member"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"54d6040a-6772-4826-b011-6efe85649b28"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMemberQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMemberQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "71dee59f-99c5-4705-9a2c-cd540c2e2b0c"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "whether a vertex list is a member of a head on a graph"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"b90a671f-1802-4c9e-9241-34adee8708cd"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Substrates and Drawing", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"c7d8cc2b-1d19-4d7c-898e-ba84f2b752e3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraSubstrate"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSubstrate", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "7c5a1f9a-f284-4e50-ac3e-b097c8e39c7e"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the named example substrates at size \"Small\", \"Medium\" or \"Large\": \
the tilings, meshes and closed surfaces the other pages draw on; \
InfraSubstrate[] lists the roster"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"5fd7e065-8c33-4bcb-b0ca-f7bd1e1b781a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraSubstrateHighlight"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSubstrateHighlight", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "534e3460-f297-4606-a7b6-ab53b76ffa97"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the summed densities of a list of objects drawn on a graph, the i-th object \
in the i-th palette color; a Directive styles the objects after it"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"14073023-54b2-4a6b-9169-8826ee84684f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Multi-constructions", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"393a64cc-2049-48ed-b14b-6171dba22715"],

Cell["\<\
Whereas the causal graph of Euclidean constructions is causally invariant, \
the branchial graphs in infrageometry are non-trivial due to \
multi-constructions.\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"58384326-f8ca-4f7d-860f-22814669d418"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraScene"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraScene", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "392336b6-c5b7-4e0b-b4ad-81f76e88d11c"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a construction stated before any graph: the objects, and hypotheses that \
construct them with inert heads or assert relations between them"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"d87148a5-6618-41dc-a25e-f2b71c8c1f72"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraStep"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraStep", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "53d6e57a-a7ff-42b5-a2bb-2ef0c9c777c6"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one construction encapsulated as a step of a scene; a second argument \
labels it"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"3dd8d983-39fe-484d-8083-d55dbc1fb361"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraScene"]], 
